---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/layout/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import { COMPANY } from "../../data/company";
const lastUpdated = "2026-05-21";
---

<Layout title="CCPA / California Privacy Rights | Cliffco" description={`${COMPANY.brandName} California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) and California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA) notice.`}>
  <Breadcrumbs trail={[
    { name: "Home", href: "/" },
    { name: "Legal", href: "/legal/" },
    { name: "CCPA", href: "/legal/ccpa/" },
  ]} />

  <section class="container-prose pt-12 pb-16">
    <h1 style="font-size: var(--text-display-lg);">California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA) Disclosure</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-muted)] mt-2">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p class="mt-6">
      This notice supplements our <a href="/legal/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> and applies to
      California residents under the California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA), as amended by the
      California Privacy Rights Act (CPRA). {COMPANY.legalName} has implemented procedures to
      ensure that California residents are afforded the rights described below.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10">California Resident Rights Under the CCPA</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Right to know:</strong> The right to know, both by category and by specific pieces
        of information, what personal information is collected, used, shared, or sold about you.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Right to delete:</strong> Consumers can generally demand that the Company, as well
        as its business service providers, delete personal information that is retained by the
        business. If you make a request to delete information, we may require verification of your
        identity and a confirmation that you would like your data deleted. The Company is not
        required to delete information where the information is needed in order to provide a service
        requested by the consumer, if the Company has a regulatory requirement to retain the data,
        or if we need to maintain the data for any legal or regulatory purposes.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Right to correct:</strong> Request correction of inaccurate personal information
        we hold about you.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Right to opt out of sale or sharing:</strong> The right to opt out of the sale of
        personal information. Note that Cliffco does not sell personal information.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Right to access:</strong> The right to obtain a free copy of all personal
        information collected about you by the Company, which we share after verifying your identity.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Right to limit use of sensitive personal information.</strong>
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Right to equal service and pricing:</strong> The Company will not deny any goods or
        services to a consumer who chooses to exercise his or her rights under the CCPA.
        Additionally, we will not charge or propose that a consumer receive different prices or
        rates for goods or services, or a different level or quality of service, or take any other
        measures to discriminate against a consumer for exercising his or her rights under the CCPA.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10">How to Exercise Your Rights</h2>

    <p>
      If you are a California resident, you can exercise any of the rights set forth above or
      submit any questions pertaining to this CCPA Privacy Notice by:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>Calling a Cliffco customer service representative at <a href={`tel:${COMPANY.hq.phoneE164}`}>{COMPANY.hq.phone}</a></li>
      <li>Sending an email to <a href="mailto:klovece@cliffcomortgage.com">klovece@cliffcomortgage.com</a> (ATTN: Kathleen Lovece)</li>
      <li>
        Mailing us at: {COMPANY.hq.street}, {COMPANY.hq.city}, {COMPANY.hq.region} {COMPANY.hq.postalCode},
        ATTN: Kathleen Lovece
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p class="mt-4">
      You may also appoint a natural person or business entity registered with the Secretary of
      State to exercise your rights under the CCPA, so long as you have authorized that person or
      entity to act on your behalf. We will verify your identity before responding to any request.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10">Categories of Personal Information We Collect</h2>

    <p>
      Cliffco collects personal information for a variety of reasons, including to provide
      individual financial products and services to customers. Below are the categories of personal
      information we collect that relate to, describe, identify, or could reasonably be linked,
      directly or indirectly, with you:
    </p>

    <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
        <thead>
          <tr class="bg-[var(--color-mist-gray)]">
            <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-semibold border border-[var(--color-soft-gray)] w-1/3">Category</th>
            <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 font-semibold border border-[var(--color-soft-gray)]">Examples</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 border border-[var(--color-soft-gray)] align-top font-medium">Personal Unique Identifiers</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 border border-[var(--color-soft-gray)]">Full name, address, email address, Social Security number, etc.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="bg-[var(--color-mist-gray)]/40">
            <td class="px-4 py-3 border border-[var(--color-soft-gray)] align-top font-medium">Personal Information</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 border border-[var(--color-soft-gray)]">Financial account numbers, credit scores, phone number, etc.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 border border-[var(--color-soft-gray)] align-top font-medium">Purchase Information</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 border border-[var(--color-soft-gray)]">Records of personal property, products or services purchased, obtained or considered, and other purchasing histories such as account number, property details, etc.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="bg-[var(--color-mist-gray)]/40">
            <td class="px-4 py-3 border border-[var(--color-soft-gray)] align-top font-medium">Protected Classifications</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 border border-[var(--color-soft-gray)]">Marital status, sex, racial or ethnic origin, etc.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 border border-[var(--color-soft-gray)] align-top font-medium">Internet / Browsing Activity</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 border border-[var(--color-soft-gray)]">IP address, browsing history, information regarding interaction with our websites, advertisements, etc.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="bg-[var(--color-mist-gray)]/40">
            <td class="px-4 py-3 border border-[var(--color-soft-gray)] align-top font-medium">Professional / Employment-Related Information</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-3 border border-[var(--color-soft-gray)]">Employment history, income information, and related records provided during the loan application process.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2 class="mt-10">How We Collect Personal Information</h2>

    <p>
      We collect personal information from California residents both directly and indirectly,
      depending on our relationship with the specific individual.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-4 font-medium">We collect personal information directly from sources such as:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Paper or electronic applications for a loan, where you provide information such as employment history, contact information, income information, etc.</li>
      <li>Telephone conversations that you have with employees of Cliffco.</li>
      <li>Interactions that you have with our website, social media, advertisements, etc.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="mt-4 font-medium">We also collect personal information indirectly from sources such as:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Third-party service providers that provide data to support activities like fraud prevention, marketing, etc.</li>
      <li>Social media websites.</li>
      <li>Government entities that provide public records.</li>
      <li>Consumer data resellers.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10">How We Use Personal Information</h2>

    <p>We use the personal information that we collect in a variety of ways, including:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Managing and delivering the services that you have engaged us to provide.</li>
      <li>Improving user experiences through research on marketing, developing and improving products and services.</li>
      <li>Addressing security issues or system integrity.</li>
      <li>Supporting everyday business operations such as monitoring, reporting, accounting, and enabling use of service providers for business purposes.</li>
      <li>Ensuring compliance with our legal and regulatory obligations, such as assisting with legal requests and demands, responding to audit requests, and enabling information security.</li>
      <li>Conducting other legitimate and lawful business purposes.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10">Categories of Third Parties to Whom We Disclose Personal Information</h2>

    <p>
      {COMPANY.legalName} does not sell your personal information. However, we may share personal
      information with third parties. The categories of third parties with whom we share personal
      information include:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Government agencies.</li>
      <li>Application vendors.</li>
      <li>Third-party service providers.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="mt-10">Changes to This CCPA Privacy Notice</h2>

    <p>
      We may make changes to this CCPA Privacy Notice from time to time. We will inform you of
      changes by posting the revised notice on our website with a revised "Last Updated" date.
      Unless otherwise stated, the revised notice is effective as of the date it is posted.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>
